First Author: Allehyani
Title: Machine learning approach to predict 1-year mortality after heart transplantation: a single-centre study
Source number: 59

Very short summary: This retrospective single-centre study included 419 heart transplant recipients treated in Saudi Arabia between 2007 and 2022. Support vector machine (SVM) and logistic regression (LR) models were evaluated for predicting 1-year mortality; the SVM achieved a held-out test AUC of 0.868, accuracy of 95.24%, precision of 90%, and recall of 75%, while LR performed slightly better overall.

